Subject: [PATCH 0012] Prism: full Chrome profile import (Phase 6)

chrome://prism-welcome's "Import from Chrome" now inherits Chrome's login
state instead of only bookmarks/history:
- chrome/browser/prism/prism_chrome_importer.{h,mm} (src-overlay): copies the
  "Chrome Safe Storage" keychain seed into "Prism Safe Storage" (one
  interactive ACL prompt — user-present by design) and stages Cookies /
  Login Data / Preferences / Secure Preferences / Extensions into
  <user-data-dir>/PrismChromeImport.staging/. SQLite payloads are copied
  with their WAL sidecars and integrity-checked on the staged copy, so a
  running Chrome is safe. Chrome's own directory is read-only throughout.
- chrome_browser_main.cc: ApplyStagedChromeImport() runs from
  PreMainMessageLoopRunImpl, moving the staged files into the Default
  profile before any service opens them (an in-place copy would be
  clobbered on shutdown). OSCrypt then derives its key from the migrated
  seed (same PBKDF2 chain as Chrome's, patch 0004), so the copied v10
  ciphertexts decrypt transparently.
- ui/BUILD.gn: compile the importer (mac-only, like the rest of the Prism
  chrome layer). Inserted past patch 0011's hunk context so the series
  stays individually reverse-applicable.

Test hooks (used by the fixture test, documented in
docs/chrome-import.md): --prism-chrome-profile-dir,
--prism-import-keychain-read-from, --prism-import-keychain-write-to.
